---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import me2 from "../assets/me/skiing.png";
import me3 from "../assets/me/troll.jpg";
import me4 from "../assets/me/first_phone.jpg";

const lastmod = "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z";
const photoSizes = "(min-width: 1184px) 536px, (min-width: 801px) calc(50vw - 56px), (min-width: 701px) calc(100vw - 64px), calc(100vw - 40px)";
const photoWidths = [320, 480, 640, 960, 1280];
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="A look behind the screen — what drives me, what I value, and what I tinker with."
  lastmod={lastmod}
>
  <h1>whoami</h1>
  <p class="full-width">
    I'm Arttu - a developer from Finland with a background in computer science
    and eCommerce development. This page is a more personal look at what I do
    outside of work and what keeps me curious. While my <a href="/experience/"
      >Experience</a
    > page covers the professional side, this one's about the hobbies, interests,
    and values that shape how I think and work.
  </p>

  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>Hobbies & Interests</h2>

      <p>
        I have a lot of hobbies. Listing all of them would take a while, so
        here are the ones I spend the most time on.
      </p>

      <p>
        The newest is Magic: The Gathering, which I started playing in early
        2026. I'm enjoying getting to know the lore, learning the rules, and
        discovering the cards. There's a lot to take in. Luckily, I enjoy
        that part too.
      </p>

      <p>
        I started DJ'ing in March 2025. I'm still learning, but I love finding
        good music, working out how tracks fit together, and meeting people
        who share the interest.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've also picked up running again after a long break. Slowly trying
        to get back into the shape I was in ten years ago. Getting there.
      </p>

      <p>
        In summer, I like to go magnet fishing with friends. Low effort,
        weirdly satisfying. It feels like a treasure hunt, even when the
        treasure turns out to be another rusty bit of metal.
      </p>

      <p>
        I read a lot too, mostly biographies, tech history, and the occasional
        obscure topic. For <a href="https://letterboxd.com/narttu/">movies and
        TV shows</a>, I usually gravitate towards sci-fi, thrillers, horror,
        or anime.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-image">
      <div class="about-photo" style={`aspect-ratio:${me2.width} / ${me2.height}`}>
        <Image src={me2} alt="Me skiing." widths={photoWidths} sizes={photoSizes} loading="eager" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <span>Rare photo of me skiing.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-section reverse">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>Tech & Tinkering</h2>

      <p>
        I started coding as a kid, back when websites had table layouts and
        blinking text. My first projects were simple HTML and CSS sites and
        small 2D games made with CoolBasic. None of them survived. I kind of
        wish they did.
      </p>

      <p>
        I'm interested in tech history: why VHS beat Betamax, what happened
        to Symbian, and how people's decisions shape the technology we end
        up using. That curiosity also led me to research obscure programming
        languages for my
        <a
          href="https://jyx.jyu.fi/handle/123456789/81727"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Bachelor's Thesis</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p>
        Over the years, I've tried different operating systems, run a home
        Linux server, and started countless side projects. Many based on a
        joke. Most unfinished. Fun while they lasted.
        Some of the finished ones are on my <a href="/projects/">projects</a>
        page.
      </p>

      <p>
        Working and studying leaves less time for side projects these days.
        Most of my tinkering now goes into this site and trying out new
        technology and AI tools. I like keeping up with what's changing and
        finding out for myself which tools are useful.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-image">
      <div class="about-photo" style={`aspect-ratio:${me4.width} / ${me4.height}`}>
      <Image
        src={me4}
        alt="Me as a child with my first phone I got as a christmas gift."
        widths={photoWidths}
        sizes={photoSizes}
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      </div>
      <span>Me as a child with my first phone I got as a christmas gift.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="about-section">
    <div class="about-text">
      <h2>What I Value</h2>
      <p>
        I like understanding how things work, whether that's technology,
        people, systems, or stories. I learn by building, with just enough
        background to get started.
      </p>
      <p>
        I enjoy being around people who care deeply about something, whether
        it's music, insects, or obscure programming languages. Passion is cool.
      </p>
      <p>
        I value people who treat others with respect, regardless of their
        title or role. That matters to me at work and outside it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I take responsibility for my work and appreciate a sense of humour
        along the way.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-image">
      <div class="about-photo" style={`aspect-ratio:${me3.width} / ${me3.height}`}>
        <Image src={me3} alt="A troll toy holding me in its hands" widths={photoWidths} sizes={photoSizes} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
      <span>A troll toy holding me in its hands.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="hr-3" />



  <style>

.about-section { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; align-items:start; gap:3rem; padding:2.5rem 0; border-top:1px solid var(--color-outlines); margin-bottom:2rem; }
.about-section.reverse { direction:rtl; }
.about-section.reverse > * { direction:ltr; }
.about-text h2 { font-size:1.65rem; margin-bottom:1.5rem; }
.about-image { display:grid; gap:.75rem; }
.about-photo { background:var(--accent-second); border:1px solid var(--color-outlines); overflow:hidden; }
.about-image img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; }
.about-image span { font-size:.8rem; color:var(--color-muted); }
@media(max-width:800px) { .about-section,.about-section.reverse { grid-template-columns:1fr; direction:ltr; gap:1.5rem; } }

</style>
</Layout>
